ws/articles/cw62p42p288do--529dff662e52.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cw62p42p288do?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">A proposed class action claims the firm hid the impact of slowing PC sales from shareholders.</summary></entry><entry><title>Suspected China spy linked to Nvidia's ex-boss left in 2025, Megaspeed says</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cmdx1vpprk9vo#0</id><updated>2026-11-16T18:41:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T01:47:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cmdx1vpprk9vo--56dedeeec32c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cmdx1vpprk9vo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The Nvidia scandal has raised questions over whether advanced AI chips ended up in China, despite US restrictions.</summary></entry><entry><title>South Korea's top scorer in tax accountancy exam admits cheating</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ckvg2ezvpe08o#0</id><updated>2026-11-16T18:41:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T13:37:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ckvg2ezvpe08o--9a149bdd0ac6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ckvg2ezvpe08o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Han Won-seok, 34, confessed to using a hidden camera and AI to get a near-perfect mark on the significant test.</summary></entry><entry><title>Italy fines Meta €805m over accessing users' photos</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cwn83gxemk35o#0</id><updated>2026-11-16T18:41:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T18:28:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cwn83gxemk35o--d66099d92304.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cwn83gxemk35o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The social media giant is accused of not informing 20 million users it had access to their photos.</summary></entry><entry><title>Microsoft says services fully restored after day-long global outage</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c6rrg51rkz09o#0</id><updated>2026-11-16T18:41:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T06:42:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c6rrg51rkz09o--334ebcca2306.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c6rrg51rkz09o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Efforts to address the underlying problem with Outlook, Teams and Copilot are complete, the tech firm says.</summary></entry><entry><title>Even Grand Theft Auto's original creators haven't been able to play GTA 6</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c6jd7k5ryl1mo#0</id><updated>2026-11-16T18:41:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T00:37:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c6jd7k5ryl1mo--f42c8666591c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c6jd7k5ryl1mo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The next title in the series is expected to be the biggest video game release ever.</summary></entry><entry><title>How the Jensen Huang scandal created a headache for business-friendly Singapore</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ck1exevgql4qo#0</id><updated>2026-11-16T18:41:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T23:00:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ck1exevgql4qo--59d35bd98e07.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ck1exevgql4qo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The scandal has cast a spotlight on Singapore's success as a chip hub - and a location for alleged illicit trade.</summary></entry><entry><title>Microsoft outage 'stark reminder' of how much we rely on tech</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cxzd9171m51qo#0</id><updated>2026-11-16T18:41:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T21:15:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cxzd9171m51qo--d3bc368f2c82.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cxzd9171m51qo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Microsoft has apologised for the issue, which it said was due to a technical failure.</summary></entry><entry><title>Pressure grows on Trump's Commerce Secretary Lutnick in fallout from Nvidia scandal</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqvg2d1eg7zro#0</id><updated>2026-11-16T18:41:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T19:53:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqvg2d1eg7zro--c19561116954.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqvg2d1eg7zro?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Scott Bessent told CNBC that several government agencies "were in favour of putting Megaspeed on the entity list for months".</summary></entry><entry><title>Why is Microsoft's outage lasting so long and will emails be lost?</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cwvg238zrnm5o#0</id><updated>2026-11-16T18:41:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T18:36:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cwvg238zrnm5o--f83f812563eb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cwvg238zrnm5o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Microsoft says it is continuing to restore services including Outlook and Teams following a global outage.</summary></entry><entry><title>Courts, spies and MPs: How the Microsoft outage has been felt around the world</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqp9d58eldlro#0</id><updated>2026-11-16T18